{
  "version": "1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "can-bus",
    "description": "CAN transport demo on the in-process VIRTUAL adapter - no hardware, no Python. A UInt16 counter (Sources.Iterator) is packed into a 2-byte little-endian payload by Bytes.Pack and built into CAN frames by two Can.Encode nodes (IDs 0x100 and 0x200, set via each encoder's 'defaults' id). Both transmit on 'virtual:bus0' through Can.Bus. A second Can.Bus on the same virtual bus (listen-only) receives every frame, Can.Filter keeps only 0x100, Can.Decode splits the frame back into id/data/dlc, and Bytes.Unpack recovers the counter for plotting and logging (a Debug.ValueDisplay also shows the raw packed bytes). Covers all CAN/Bus nodes (Can.Bus x2, Can.Encode, Can.Decode, Can.Filter) using only the byte-based nodes for data. Runs as-is; real hardware uses an adapter spec like 'socketcan:can0' or 'peak:0'.",
    "authoring": {
      "version": "1.0",
      "metadata": {
        "name": "can-bus",
        "description": "CAN transport demo on the in-process VIRTUAL adapter - no hardware, no Python. A UInt16 counter (Sources.Iterator) is packed into a 2-byte little-endian payload by Bytes.Pack and built into CAN frames by two Can.Encode nodes (IDs 0x100 and 0x200, set via each encoder's 'defaults' id). Both transmit on 'virtual:bus0' through Can.Bus. A second Can.Bus on the same virtual bus (listen-only) receives every frame, Can.Filter keeps only 0x100, Can.Decode splits the frame back into id/data/dlc, and Bytes.Unpack recovers the counter for plotting and logging (a Debug.ValueDisplay also shows the raw packed bytes). Covers all CAN/Bus nodes (Can.Bus x2, Can.Encode, Can.Decode, Can.Filter) using only the byte-based nodes for data. Runs as-is; real hardware uses an adapter spec like 'socketcan:can0' or 'peak:0'."
      },
