        {
          "id": "note-virtual",
          "type": "Note",
          "position": {
            "x": 841.748092898958,
            "y": 100.42487130112332
          },
          "width": 360,
          "height": 150,
          "config": {
            "text": "VIRTUAL (in-process) CAN bus. Every Can.Bus whose 'adapter' is 'virtual:bus0' shares one in-process bus - no hardware. Here 'can-tx' transmits and 'can-rx' (listen-only, same bus) receives. The two Can.Encode nodes send IDs 0x100 (256) and 0x200 (512); the init frame each encoder emits when its constant ID arrives carries no data and is harmless. Real adapters: 'socketcan:can0', 'peak:0'."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "note-filter",
          "type": "Note",
          "position": {
            "x": 1280,
            "y": 280
          },
          "width": 300,
          "height": 140,
          "config": {
            "text": "Can.Filter mode 'acceptIds' ids:[256] passes only 0x100 and drops 0x200. Other modes: acceptAll, rejectIds, idRange (idMin/idMax), mask (idMask/idMatch). Can.Decode then splits the frame; Bytes.Unpack reads the 2-byte little-endian counter back out of the payload."
          }
        },
        {
